{
  "_comment": "Clips keyed on the Universal Animation Library's rig (tools/blender/build_npc_clips.py; openspec/changes/npc-characters, design section 6 and task 3.2), for the clips UAL Standard lacks. Directions are [left, front, up] (the body's left, its front, up), given in the rest frame of the frame bone and turned with it as posed. Rotations are degrees about an armature axis (X: positive bends forward; Y: positive tips a left-side bone down; Z: positive turns toward the body's left), applied after the bone's parent. A motion adds a sine of deg amplitude with a whole number of cycles per clip, so every clip loops seamlessly (its last frame equals its first). Clip names end in _Loop, as UAL's looping clips do: Godot's glTF import marks those looping and strips the suffix, so the game plays them as undercity/Surrender and undercity/Cower (data/npc_bodies.json).",
